<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  RIPDPI journey: toggle the primary mode. Mirrors
  maestro/04-start-stop-configured-mode.yaml. Schema (root <journey> +
  <description> + ordered <step>) follows the Android Studio "New > Journey Test"
  template; confirm against the installed Android CLI 1.0 template before this
  lane gates merges. See journeys/README.md.
-->
<journey name="04-start-stop-configured-mode">
  <description>
    Mode-toggle smoke test: start and then stop the primary local DPI-bypass
    mode from the Home screen, verifying the UI stays consistent. Does not
    assert a live tunnel (a real VPN start raises the system consent dialog).
  </description>
  <step>Launch the RIPDPI app from a cold start (force-stop it first if running).</step>
  <step>Confirm the Home screen is displayed.</step>
  <step>Expand the "Modes &amp; diagnostics" section.</step>
  <step>Confirm the primary "Local DPI bypass" mode is visible on the Home screen.</step>
  <step>Tap the primary "Local DPI bypass" mode to start it.</step>
  <step>Confirm the primary "Local DPI bypass" mode is still visible and the Home screen reflects the change.</step>
  <step>Tap the primary "Local DPI bypass" mode again to stop it.</step>
  <step>Confirm the Home screen still shows the primary "Local DPI bypass" mode.</step>
</journey>
